# WHAT MUST NEVER ENTER AN IMAGE.
#
# The first line is the only one that would be a security incident if it were missing. `.env` holds
# DATABASE_URL and two provider keys; an image is a build artifact that gets pushed to a registry,
# pulled by a platform, and cached in layers that outlive the container. A secret baked into a layer
# is a secret you cannot revoke by editing a file.
#
# Every secret this deployment needs is set with `fly secrets set`, which stores it encrypted and
# injects it at runtime. Nothing below is copied.
#
# THE `**/` VARIANTS ARE NOT OPTIONAL (S-WEB). A bare `.env`/`.env.*` anchors to the CONTEXT ROOT, so
# a NESTED env file — `apps/web/.env.local`, which Next.js loads from the app directory — sailed past
# these two lines into the web image and baked PLAYROOM_WEB_TOKEN (a real member credential) into a
# pushed layer. The whole web tier then authenticated as `prince` for every unredeemed request, which
# is exactly the attribution WEB-1 exists to prevent. `.next` already carried its `**/` twin (below);
# `.env` did not. It does now — at every depth, both images.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Not secrets, just weight and correctness.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
.next-dev
.next-prod
**/.next
**/.next-dev
**/.next-prod
.git
.github
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The film and its assets: ~1MB of GIF and PNG that no server reads.
docs/demo/assets

# A SEPARATE PROJECT THAT LIVES INSIDE THIS WORKING TREE (S-LIVE). `packet-tracer-mcp/` is not part
# of this repository — chore 35b0abd excluded it from git and from prettier, and missed this file.
# `COPY . .` does not read .gitignore, so 70MB and 3,095 files (including a Python venv with its own
# vendored dependencies) were being uploaded as build context and baked into BOTH public images.
#
# Nothing in it is a secret — the scan before the first S-LIVE deploy found only pydantic's own
# docstrings — but a foreign project's virtualenv inside Playroom's shipped image is weight nobody
# can explain and surface nobody audited. Excluded at the boundary that actually governs the image.
packet-tracer-mcp/

# Local tooling and scratch.
.claude
coverage
*.log
